 - Write artifact-scoped CSS with custom properties for its palette, type scale, spacing rhythm, rules, and shadows. Use grid and flex intentionally, coherent readable font sizes and line heights, controlled line lengths, stable alignment, and max-content geometry where sequences must remain complete.
 - Treat short semantic labels, kickers, statuses, and categorical phrases as atomic reading units. Labels such as HYPOTHESIS, OPEN QUESTION, READINESS CHECK, and DECISION GATE must remain on one unbroken line with white-space:nowrap. Widen or recompose the surrounding columns when necessary; never split a categorical label or shrink it below the canvas legibility floor.
 - Inline label-and-copy rows must have an explicit visible gap—normally grid or flex gap, or at least 0.6em of label margin. Zero geometric intersection is not enough when adjacent words visually run together. Never concatenate a strong status label directly against its explanatory sentence or source line.
-- Every authored composition must work in both host themes. Base neutral ink, muted copy, rules, and surfaces on --northstar-ink, --northstar-muted, --northstar-line, --northstar-surface, and --northstar-surface-subtle; never redefine those host-owned token names inside an island. Create distinctly named local variables only for intentional accent colors, and keep those accents accessible in both modes. The renderer supplies reversible dark counterparts for legacy hard-coded neutrals. Use data-canvas-v2-theme-preserve="true" only for a deliberate brand swatch or visual whose literal color must never adapt.
+- Every authored composition must work in both host themes. Base neutral ink, muted copy, rules, and surfaces on --northstar-ink, --northstar-muted, --northstar-line, --northstar-surface, and --northstar-surface-subtle; never redefine those host-owned token names inside an island. Every local solid accent must remain readable against its actual surface in both modes—not merely exist as the same hex value twice. Prefer explicit light/dark local variables selected through :root[data-canvas-v2-theme="dark"] when the palette meaningfully changes. The native renderer still evaluates every solid foreground, surface, border, caret, SVG fill, and SVG stroke at the final render boundary, preserving compatible color and deriving a reversible counterpart when contrast fails. Give every meaningful painted mark a stable native element rather than hiding it in ::before or ::after. Use data-canvas-v2-theme-preserve="true" only on a leaf-level literal brand swatch or media visual whose exact source color is itself the evidence; never use it to exempt readable copy, a whole island, or a container subtree.
 - Any empty field, card, cell, note, lane, or block that visually invites the person to write must be one stable native object carrying data-canvas-v2-writable="true" and a descriptive aria-label. Keep the writable surface itself empty and leaf-level; labels and instructions belong in separate identified siblings. Never draw a fake input, blank card, or workshop writing area that cannot be selected and edited. Decorative rules, backgrounds, charts, and relationship geometry must not carry writable semantics.
 - Establish a small number of strong alignment rails and one unmistakable primary anchor. Related elements should share edges, baselines, centers, or a declared visual axis; near-misses look accidental.
 - Use a repeatable spacing rhythm with deliberate exceptions. Dense evidence may be compact, but narrative transitions need enough air to make the reading order obvious.
